    "tactics": "Owlbears charge aggressively, attempting to trigger Aggressive Charge to knock prey prone. They use Multiattack every round, trying to trigger Maul for devastating damage. Wounded owlbears become frenzied and reckless.",
    "attacksNotes": "<p>Beak [Combat]: Melee attack (Agil 7 + Melee Combat 5), Reach: 10 ft (Large creature)</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Margin 1:</strong>: 15 damage (10 + 5 Str)</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 2:</strong> 15 damage, DR halved (round up)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Claws [Combat]: Melee attack (Agil 7 + Melee Combat 5 vs opponent's defense), Reach: 10 ft (Large creature)</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Margin 1:</strong>: 15 damage (10 + 5 Str)</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 2:</strong> 15 damage, DR halved (round up)</li>\n</ul>",
    "specialAbilitiesNotes": "<p>Large <strong>Size:</strong> Occupies 10×10 ft space, 10 ft reach Keen Sight and Smell: Vision and scent-based Perception checks have Fortune Maul: If both ### Attacks (beak AND claw) hit the same target in one turn, target takes additional 4 damage (no attribute modifier, represents crushing embrace) Aggressive Charge (Recharge 6-8): If the owlbear moves at least 20 feet straight toward a target and then hits with a claw attack on the same turn, the target must make a Fortitude [Easy] save or be knocked Prone. If prone, owlbear can immediately make a beak attack as a [Free] action.</p>",
